---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">WT / AI-Native Offensive Security Research</p>
    <h1>Understand infrastructure.<br />Discover vulnerabilities.<br />Advance security.</h1>
    <p class="lead">WhateverTakes is a four-member offensive security research team studying the software and systems that power enterprise infrastructure. We combine AI-driven research automation with human technical understanding, independent verification and continuous improvement.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/research/">Research direction</a><a class="button" href="/blog/">Research blog</a></div>
  </section>
  <p class="eyebrow">Research areas</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <section class="panel"><h3>01 / Infrastructure</h3><p>Architecture, internals and security boundaries of operating systems, networks, virtualization, containers and cloud infrastructure.</p></section>
    <section class="panel"><h3>02 / Vulnerability research</h3><p>Authorized security research on open-source and commercial infrastructure products, with coordinated disclosure.</p></section>
    <section class="panel"><h3>03 / AI-native security engineering</h3><p>AI agents and validated tools for research, development and experimentation, with human oversight and reproducible evidence.</p></section>
  </div>
  <h2>Our research philosophy</h2>
  <p class="lead">AI executes. Humans understand, verify, and advance.</p>
  <p>We pursue original vulnerability discoveries, eligible bug bounties and accepted open-source security contributions, without claiming outcomes before they are confirmed.</p>
  <h2>Selected project</h2>
  <div class="panel"><h3><a href="https://github.com/whatevertakes/CTF-OS">CTF-OS ↗</a></h3><p>Challenge-scoped Codex engine for human-selected CTF problems in isolated environments. Competition performance is not yet established.</p></div>
  <h2>Meet the team</h2><p>Four researchers, individual technical blogs documenting understanding and improvements, and a shared research direction.</p><a href="/members/">Team profiles →</a>
</Base>
